{
    "title": "CCC: Call of the Giant Eagle",
    "description": "Meet Alex and his friends Poppy and Niko. As members of the\r\nCurious Critters Club, they are dedicated to the task of discovering\r\nnew critters for science. Sometimes the creatures turn out to be\r\nextraordinary!\r\n\r\nOne day in the forests of New Zealand, the group discover damage\r\nto the trees and hear strange sounds. Could it be Te Hokioi, the\r\ngiant eagle? Alex is eager to know and is soon hot on the trail. But\r\nwhat he discovers are a different kind of curious critter. Ones that\r\nuse mechanical machines to do their destructive deeds. Luckily\r\nAlex has a plan, but will it be enough to save the forest?\r\n\r\nThis exciting interactive book is loaded with interactivity, animation,\r\nmusic and sound on every page. It also features a range of options\r\nwhich allows you to experience the book in a style that suits you\r\nbest.\r\n\r\nSTORY HIGHLIGHTS\r\n\r\n\u2022 Your interactions drives the story forward\r\n\u2022 Tilt your device for a 3D parallax effect\r\n\u2022 Words appear as they are narrated\r\n\u2022 Fantastic illustrations and animation\r\n\u2022 Original music and sound\r\n\u2022 Story told by NZ performer, Madeleine Sami\r\n\u2022 Narration options: English and French\r\n\u2022 Toggle narration, text and audio\r\n\u2022 App is free-to-play, optimised for phones and tablets\r\n\u2022 Intuitive, kid-friendly navigation\r\n\r\nCHILD FRIENDLY\r\n\r\n\u2022 Parental controls\r\n\u2022 No advertisements\r\n\u2022 No in-app purchases\r\n\u2022 No location data collected\r\n\u2022 No social links\r\n\r\nCURIOUS CRITTERS CLUB - THE SERIES\r\nFind more FREE Curious Critters Club stories and AR, online\r\ngames at:\r\nwww.curiouscrittersclub.com\r\n\r\nCreated by Yoozoo ltd and La bo\u00eete \u00e0 pitons.\r\nMade with the assistance of NZ On Air and the Canadian Media\r\nFund.",
    "descriptionHTML": "Meet Alex and his friends Poppy and Niko. As members of the<br>Curious Critters Club, they are dedicated to the task of discovering<br>new critters for science. Sometimes the creatures turn out to be<br>extraordinary!<br><br>One day in the forests of New Zealand, the group discover damage<br>to the trees and hear strange sounds. Could it be Te Hokioi, the<br>giant eagle? Alex is eager to know and is soon hot on the trail. But<br>what he discovers are a different kind of curious critter. Ones that<br>use mechanical machines to do their destructive deeds. Luckily<br>Alex has a plan, but will it be enough to save the forest?<br><br>This exciting interactive book is loaded with interactivity, animation,<br>music and sound on every page. It also features a range of options<br>which allows you to experience the book in a style that suits you<br>best.<br><br>STORY HIGHLIGHTS<br><br>\u2022 Your interactions drives the story forward<br>\u2022 Tilt your device for a 3D parallax effect<br>\u2022 Words appear as they are narrated<br>\u2022 Fantastic illustrations and animation<br>\u2022 Original music and sound<br>\u2022 Story told by NZ performer, Madeleine Sami<br>\u2022 Narration options: English and French<br>\u2022 Toggle narration, text and audio<br>\u2022 App is free-to-play, optimised for phones and tablets<br>\u2022 Intuitive, kid-friendly navigation<br><br>CHILD FRIENDLY<br><br>\u2022 Parental controls<br>\u2022 No advertisements<br>\u2022 No in-app purchases<br>\u2022 No location data collected<br>\u2022 No social links<br><br>CURIOUS CRITTERS CLUB - THE SERIES<br>Find more FREE Curious Critters Club stories and AR, online<br>games at:<br>www.curiouscrittersclub.com<br><br>Created by Yoozoo ltd and La bo\u00eete \u00e0 pitons.<br>Made with the assistance of NZ On Air and the Canadian Media<br>Fund.",
